ferential equation:\n\n$$\n3{\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n(n-1){a}_{n}{x}^{n-2}+{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the first sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n-2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n3{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }(m+2)(m+1){a}_{m+2}{x}^{m}+{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}=0.\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in the first summation (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n3{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}{x}^{n}+{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}=0.\n$$\n\nSince both sums now start with $n=0,$ we can combine them as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }[3(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}+{a}_{n}]{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nSetting each coefficient of $x$ equal to zero, we obtain\n\n$$\n3(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}+{a}_{n}=0.\n$$\n\nFinally, the recursion formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+2}=-\\frac{{a}_{n}}{3(n+1)(n+2)},\\,n=0,1,2,…\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(n)=-3(n+1)(n+2).$" 13194139534875 true] [17592186316747 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316748 13194139534875 true] [17592186316747 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316749 13194139534875 true] [17592186316747 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316750 13194139534875 true] [17592186316747 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316751 13194139534875 true] [17592186316747 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316752 13194139534875 true] [17592186316747 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534875 true] [17592186316747 1041 "selection" 13194139534875 true] [17592186316747 1104 #edb/ref 17592186316748 13194139534875 true] [17592186316747 1110 #uuid "86b841a0-6081-523b-8721-72c7e84cda0b" 13194139534875 true] [17592186316748 1034 "f(n)=-3(n+1)(n+2)" 13194139534875 true] [17592186316748 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534875 true] [17592186316748 1111 #uuid "38613dba-7e75-52bc-8e63-ae8a21f22187" 13194139534875 true] [17592186316749 1034 "f(n)=-n(n+3)" 13194139534875 true] [17592186316749 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534875 true] [17592186316749 1111 #uuid "d2a78034-d04d-5bf2-92de-eacbf4e23d5f" 13194139534875 true] [17592186316750 1034 "f(n)=-3n(3n+1)" 13194139534875 true] [17592186316750 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534875 true] [17592186316750 1111 #uuid "324aa07a-a79a-50ca-a282-6966c9a15158" 13194139534875 true] [17592186316751 1034 "f(n)=3(n+2)(n+3)" 13194139534875 true] [17592186316751 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534875 true] [17592186316751 1111 #uuid "045588b0-7288-5a91-9d78-5fcbcfc05ed8" 13194139534875 true] [17592186316752 1034 "f(n)=n(2n+3)" 13194139534875 true] [17592186316752 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534875 true] [17592186316752 1111 #uuid "8acd55b2-407f-5637-810e-b977ac1dd1a6" 13194139534875 true] [17592186316753 1017 #edb/ref 17592186316754 13194139534875 true] [17592186316753 1089 "q-64536" 13194139534875 true] [17592186316753 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534875 true] [17592186316753 1100 "Let $y={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a series solution to the equation ${y}^{′}+7xy=0.$\n\nWhat is the recurrence relation for the coefficients ${a}_{n},$ where $n=1,2,3,…$" 13194139534875 true] [17592186316753 1113 #uuid "410df22e-fae0-5291-8e4b-8ae39b283772" 13194139534875 true] [17592186316753 1145 "First, we find ${y}^{′}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the expressions for $y(x)$ and ${y}^{′}(x)$ into the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}+7x{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n} & =0 \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}+7{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the first sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n-1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }(m+1){a}_{m+1}{x}^{m}+7{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1}=0.\n$$\n\nNow, in the second series, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n+1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }(m+1){a}_{m+1}{x}^{m}+7{\\sum }_{m=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{m-1}{x}^{m}=0.\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in both summations (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}+7{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n-1}{x}^{n}=0.\n$$\n\nNext, we need to get two series starting with the same value of $n.$ So, we take out the term $n=0$ from the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}+7{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n-1}{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nWe now combine the series, as follows:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }[(n+1){a}_{n+1}+7{a}_{n-1}]{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nFinally, by equating coefficients of ${x}^{n},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=0,\\,(n+1){a}_{n+1}=-7{a}_{n-1}.\n$$\n\nSolving for ${a}_{n+1}$ gives\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{7{a}_{n-1}}{n+1},\\,n=1,2,3,….\n$$\n\nNote that every coefficient with an odd index is equal to $0,$ since ${a}_{1}=0.$" 13194139534875 true] [17592186316754 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316755 13194139534875 true] [17592186316754 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316756 13194139534875 true] [17592186316754 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316757 13194139534875 true] [17592186316754 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316758 13194139534875 true] [17592186316754 1000 #edb/ref 17592186316759 13194139534875 true] [17592186316754 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534875 true] [17592186316754 1041 "selection" 13194139534875 true] [17592186316754 1104 #edb/ref 17592186316759 13194139534875 true] [17592186316754 1110 #uuid "cdcc0029-6c41-5f3d-87ce-0cfdf54aaf58" 13194139534875 true] [17592186316755 1034 "{a}_{n+1}=7n{a}_{n}" 13194139534875 true] [17592186316755 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534875 true] [17592186316755 1111 #uuid "71dad90f-280e-5dee-9ce4-e5faaa1ff6e9" 13194139534875 true] [17592186316756 1034 "{a}_{n+1}=-7n{a}_{n-1}" 13194139534875 true] [17592186316756 1103 #edb/r